{
  "manufacturer": "Seneca",
  "manufacturer_slug": "seneca",
  "model": "R-16DI-8DO Ethernet I/O (16 digital inputs, 8 digital outputs)",
  "model_slug": "r-16di-8do",
  "short_model": "R-16DI-8DO",
  "aliases": [
    "R16DI8DO",
    "R-16DI-8DO",
    "Seneca R series 16DI 8DO"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (remote I/O module, digital inputs/outputs)",
  "applies_to": "R-16DI-8DO in the Series R I/O manual MI-00604-29-EN.",
  "summary": "The R-16DI-8DO is a Seneca R-series remote I/O with 16 digital inputs, each with a 32-bit counter and pulse timing, and 8 digital outputs. It serves Modbus TCP on two Ethernet ports and Modbus RTU on RS-485. This map covers the input and output words, counters and counter reset, low/high time and period floats, integer frequencies, and the coil/discrete-input views.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP",
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 38400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Holding-register tables print the 4x number (40001) and the 0-based offset (0); coils print 1 / offset 0 and discrete inputs 10001 / offset 0. The offset is the wire address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Series R I/O with protocol - User Manual",
    "doc_number": "MI-00604-29-EN",
    "revision_date": "2026-09-03",
    "url": "https://www.seneca.it/media/6848135/mi00604-29-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Modbus conventions pp. 95-100; R-16DI-8DO tables pp. 131-168; defaults in the web-server chapter pp. 36-41"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The protocol page lists function codes 01, 03, 05, 06, 15 and 16; the tables also give the digital inputs as 1x input status read with function 02. Modbus RTU runs on RS-485 and Modbus TCP serves up to 8 clients.",
    "Unlike some sibling R-series products, this table marks every 32-bit pair LSW first (counter 1 LSW at 40103, MSW at 40104), so counters and floats are CDAB.",
    "Factory settings from the manual: static IP 192.168.90.101/24, gateway 192.168.90.1, Modbus TCP port 502, station address 1; RS-485 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, address 1.",
    "Left out: the command register 40017 (codes not listed for this product); the 32-bit integer low/high/period copies at 40201-40296, whose unit is printed as [ms*10] and is unclear; the consecutive copy block from 48001 (it repeats the values with integer timing in 50 us steps); float frequencies at 48331+.",
    "Coils 1-16 in the coil table mirror the inputs read-only and are not listed; use discrete inputs 10001-10016."
  ],
